 "chapters": [
  {
   "title": "THE STORE",
   "mood": "comic",
   "set": [
    "R",
    3
   ],
   "lines": [
    {
     "say": "Meet my bank account which right now holds four dollars and it is the most loyal thing in my life.",
     "gag": true,
     "show": [
      {
       "v": "shot",
       "shot": "R"
      },
      {
       "on": "four",
       "v": "count",
       "to": 4,
       "prefix": "$",
       "color": "green"
      },
      {
       "on": "loyal",
       "v": "pose",
       "pose": "grin_cheer"
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "say": "Rent is due on Friday and I am out of toilet paper so I walk into the store.",
     "show": [
      {
       "v": "shot",
       "shot": "R",
       "from": 5
      },
      {
       "on": "toilet",
       "v": "text",
       "text": "OUT OF TOILET PAPER",
       "color": "white"
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "say": "The big pack is cheaper per roll but it costs more today and today I have four dollars.",
     "gag": true,
     "show": [
      {
       "v": "shot",
       "shot": "P"
      },
      {
       "on": "cheaper",
       "v": "text",
       "text": "BIG PACK = CHEAPER",
       "color": "green"
      },
      {
       "on": "today",
       "v": "text",
       "text": "BUT NOT TODAY",
       "color": "red"
      },
      {
       "on": "four",
       "v": "pose",
       "pose": "neutral_shrug"
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "say": "So I buy the small pack and I just paid extra for being broke.",
     "punch": true,
     "show": [
      {
       "v": "pose",
       "pose": "think_think"
      },
      {
       "on": "extra",
       "v": "stamp",
       "text": "PAID EXTRA"
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "say": "Researchers at the University of Michigan checked this and poor families pay about five and a half percent more for every roll.",
     "src": "S4",
     "show": [
      {
       "v": "shot",
       "shot": "P",
       "from": 3
      },
      {
       "on": "five",
       "v": "count",
       "to": 5.5,
       "dec": 1,
       "suffix": "% MORE PER ROLL",
       "color": "yellow"
      },
      {
       "on": "every",
       "v": "still",
       "shot": "P",
       "t": 4,
       "pose": "shock_panic"
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "say": "Rich families catch the sale more often because they have spare cash on the day the sale happens.",
     "src": "S4",
     "show": [
      {
       "v": "home",
       "pose": "determined_present"
      },
      {
       "v": "bars",
       "rows": [
        [
         "rich families buy on sale",
         39,
         "green"
        ],
        [
         "poor families buy on sale",
         28,
         "red"
        ]
       ]
      },
      {
       "on": "spare",
       "v": "text",
       "text": "IT IS ABOUT SPARE CASH",
       "color": "yellow"
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "say": "It is not that poor people are bad at math because the math is easy when you have the money.",
     "src": "S4",
     "show": [
      {
       "v": "pose",
       "pose": "smug_point_you"
      },
      {
       "on": "math",
       "v": "burst",
       "word": "MATH OK."
      },
      {
       "on": "easy",
       "v": "pose",
       "pose": "determined_point_l"
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "say": "And a few cents on toilet paper sounds tiny until you see what the bank does with the same four dollars.",
     "gag": true,
     "open": [
      "L3"
     ],
     "show": [
      {
       "v": "still",
       "shot": "R",
       "t": 2,
       "pose": "think_think"
      },
      {
       "on": "bank",
       "v": "shot",
       "shot": "G"
      }
     ]
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "title": "THE BANK",
   "mood": "tense",
   "set": [
    "G",
    3
   ],
   "lines": [
    {
     "say": "I walk into the bank to open a savings account like a responsible adult.",
     "show": [
      {
       "v": "shot",
       "shot": "G"
      },
      {
       "on": "savings",
       "v": "text",
       "text": "OPEN A SAVINGS ACCOUNT",
       "color": "white"
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "say": "The paper says I need five hundred dollars just to keep the account free.",
     "show": [
      {
       "v": "shot",
       "shot": "D"
      },
      {
       "on": "five",
       "v": "count",
       "to": 500,
       "prefix": "$",
       "suffix": " MINIMUM",
       "color": "red"
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "say": "That is the number one reason people in America have no bank account at all.",
     "src": "S3",
     "show": [
      {
       "v": "macro",
       "lines": [
        "Most cited reason for not having a bank account",
        "Don't have [enough money to meet minimum balance] requirements",
        "2023 FDIC National Survey"
       ],
       "far": [
        "Unbanked and Underbanked Households",
        "Executive Summary"
       ]
      },
      {
       "on": "america",
       "v": "count",
       "to": 5.6,
       "dec": 1,
       "suffix": " MILLION HOUSEHOLDS",
       "color": "yellow"
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "say": "So I keep my account with no minimum and then my card goes one dollar below zero.",
     "show": [
      {
       "v": "shot",
       "shot": "D",
       "from": 4
      },
      {
       "on": "below",
       "v": "text",
       "text": "-$1",
       "color": "red",
       "size": 200
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "say": "Have a guess what one dollar below zero costs me.",
     "punch": true,
     "show": [
      {
       "v": "pose",
       "pose": "think_think"
      },
      {
       "on": "guess",
       "v": "text",
       "text": "HAVE A GUESS…",
       "color": "yellow"
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "say": "Thirty five dollars for a one dollar mistake.",
     "show": [
      {
       "v": "shot",
       "shot": "F"
      },
      {
       "on": "thirty",
       "v": "count",
       "to": 35,
       "prefix": "$",
       "suffix": " FEE",
       "color": "red"
      },
      {
       "on": "mistake",
       "v": "sfx",
       "sound": "fail"
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "say": "Banks in America collected five point eight billion dollars from fees like this in one year.",
     "src": "S1",
     "show": [
      {
       "v": "shot",
       "shot": "T"
      },
      {
       "on": "five",
       "v": "count",
       "to": 5.8,
       "dec": 1,
       "prefix": "$",
       "suffix": " BILLION",
       "color": "green"
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "say": "And here is the twist because back in twenty nineteen it was almost twelve billion.",
     "src": "S1",
     "show": [
      {
       "v": "shot",
       "shot": "T",
       "from": 6
      },
      {
       "on": "twelve",
       "v": "count",
       "to": 11.96,
       "dec": 2,
       "prefix": "$",
       "suffix": " BILLION IN 2019",
       "color": "yellow"
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "say": "Rules and public anger cut it in half and the average family that overdrafts now keeps about one hundred eighty five dollars a year.",
     "src": "S1",
     "show": [
      {
       "v": "home",
       "pose": "grin_cheer"
      },
      {
       "v": "bars",
       "rows": [
        [
         "2019 fees (billion $)",
         11.96,
         "red"
        ],
        [
         "2023 fees (billion $)",
         5.83,
         "green"
        ]
       ]
      },
      {
       "on": "half",
       "v": "text",
       "text": "CUT IN HALF",
       "color": "green"
      },
      {
       "on": "hundred",
       "v": "count",
       "to": 185,
       "prefix": "+$",
       "suffix": " A YEAR",
       "color": "green"
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "say": "Good news for my four dollars except that when the bank says no there is another door right across the street.",
     "gag": true,
     "open": [
      "L4"
     ],
     "show": [
      {
       "v": "pose",
       "pose": "grin_cheer"
      },
      {
       "on": "except",
       "v": "pose",
       "pose": "shock_panic"
      },
      {
       "on": "door",
       "v": "shot",
       "shot": "L"
      }
     ]
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "title": "THE LOAN",
   "mood": "sad",
   "set": [
    "L",
    1
   ],
   "lines": [
    {
     "say": "Friday comes and the rent is still due and my paycheck is still a week away.",
     "show": [
      {
       "v": "shot",
       "shot": "R",
       "from": 9
      },
      {
       "on": "paycheck",
       "v": "text",
       "text": "PAYCHECK: 7 DAYS AWAY",
       "color": "yellow"
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "say": "The payday loan shop gives me cash in ten minutes and I only pay fifteen dollars for every hundred.",
     "show": [
      {
       "v": "shot",
       "shot": "L"
      },
      {
       "on": "fifteen",
       "v": "count",
       "to": 15,
       "prefix": "$",
       "suffix": " PER $100",
       "color": "red"
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "say": "Fifteen percent sounds like a bad deal but not a monster.",
     "punch": true,
     "show": [
      {
       "v": "pose",
       "pose": "neutral_shrug"
      },
      {
       "on": "monster",
       "v": "burst",
       "word": "RIGHT?"
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "say": "Except the loan lasts only two weeks so over a whole year that price is almost four hundred percent.",
     "src": "S2",
     "show": [
      {
       "v": "macro",
       "lines": [
        "a typical two-week payday loan with a $15 per $100 fee",
        "equates to an [annual percentage rate (APR) of almost 400%]",
        "Consumer Financial Protection Bureau"
       ],
       "far": [
        "Ask CFPB",
        "payday loan"
       ]
      },
      {
       "on": "two",
       "v": "text",
       "text": "ONLY 2 WEEKS",
       "color": "white"
      },
      {
       "on": "four",
       "v": "count",
       "to": 400,
       "suffix": "% A YEAR",
       "color": "red"
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "say": "A credit card for someone with money is around twenty and this is twenty times worse.",
     "show": [
      {
       "v": "shot",
       "shot": "L",
       "from": 6
      },
      {
       "on": "twenty",
       "n": 1,
       "v": "stamp",
       "text": "20× WORSE"
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "say": "And when the two weeks end most people do not have the money so they borrow again to pay the first loan.",
     "show": [
      {
       "v": "still",
       "shot": "L",
       "t": 9,
       "pose": "sleep_slump"
      },
      {
       "on": "borrow",
       "v": "text",
       "text": "BORROW AGAIN",
       "color": "red"
      },
      {
       "on": "first",
       "v": "text",
       "text": "TO PAY LOAN #1",
       "color": "white"
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "say": "Now I am paying a fee to pay a fee for a fee and my four dollars has left the chat.",
     "gag": true,
     "show": [
      {
       "v": "shot",
       "shot": "F",
       "from": 3
      },
      {
       "on": "four",
       "v": "pose",
       "pose": "shock_panic"
      },
      {
       "on": "chat",
       "v": "burst",
       "word": "BYE."
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "say": "So here is the toilet paper secret I promised you because it was never about the toilet paper.",
     "close": [
      "L2"
     ],
     "show": [
      {
       "v": "still",
       "shot": "P",
       "t": 4,
       "pose": "determined_present"
      },
      {
       "on": "never",
       "v": "text",
       "text": "NEVER ABOUT THE PAPER",
       "color": "yellow"
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "say": "The store and the bank and the loan shop all charge the most to the person with the least spare cash.",
     "close": [
      "L3"
     ],
     "show": [
      {
       "v": "shot",
       "shot": "W"
      },
      {
       "on": "most",
       "v": "text",
       "text": "LEAST CASH = HIGHEST PRICE",
       "color": "red"
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "say": "But there is one thing all three are scared of and it costs less than a pizza.",
     "open": [
      "L5"
     ],
     "show": [
      {
       "v": "pose",
       "pose": "smug_point_you"
      },
      {
       "on": "scared",
       "v": "burst",
       "word": "SCARED?"
      },
      {
       "on": "pizza",
       "v": "pose",
       "pose": "grin_cheer"
      }
     ]
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "title": "THE ANSWER",
   "mood": "think",
   "set": [
    "E",
    2
   ],
   "lines": [
    {
     "say": "So why does being broke cost more than being rich?",
     "show": [
      {
       "v": "shot",
       "shot": "E"
      },
      {
       "on": "broke",
       "v": "text",
       "text": "WHY?",
       "color": "yellow",
       "size": 200
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "say": "You would think the answer is just earn more money.",
     "show": [
      {
       "v": "pose",
       "pose": "determined_point_l"
      },
      {
       "on": "earn",
       "v": "text",
       "text": "EARN MORE?",
       "color": "white"
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "say": "Nope because the real price tag is not on your income but on your cushion.",
     "punch": true,
     "show": [
      {
       "v": "pose",
       "pose": "smug_point_you"
      },
      {
       "on": "nope",
       "v": "burst",
       "word": "NOPE."
      },
      {
       "on": "cushion",
       "v": "stamp",
       "text": "IT'S THE CUSHION",
       "color": "yellow"
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "say": "When you have no cushion every small problem gets sold back to you at the highest price in town.",
     "close": [
      "L1"
     ],
     "show": [
      {
       "v": "shot",
